<title>HUNGARY: Commerzbank Hungary'96 net profit HUF1.06bl.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank Hungary'96 net profit HUF1.06bl.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending on December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>						   1996	    1995</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  1,289   vs	818</p>
<p>    Net profit				1,059   vs	672</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		  75,770   vs   57,994</p>
<p>    Interest revenues		     7,372   vs    6,318</p>
<p>    Interest expenditures		 5,625   vs    4,975</p>
<p>    Net interest income		   1,747   vs    1,342</p>
<p>    Revenues from fees			372   vs	292</p>
<p>    Interbank lending		    31,219   vs   29,473</p>
<p>    Lending to clients		   23,918   vs   15,043</p>
<p>    Sources from banks		   53,632   vs   37.374</p>
<p>    Sources from clients		 13,137   vs   13,499</p>
<p>    Registered capital		    2,400   vs    2,400</p>
<p>    Shareholders' capital		 4,375   vs    3,194</p>
<p>    Subordinated capital		  3,299   vs    2,789</p>
<p>NOTE - Commerzbank (Budapest) Rt is the subsidiary of Germany's Commerzbank AG. The figures are unaudited, non-consolidated and were calculated according to the Hungarian Accounting Standard.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
